Top-level multi-line comments: only the first line is indented (at
column 0 here); interior lines are preserved verbatim, including their
own indentation and blank lines, except that trailing whitespace is
trimmed (fmt.indent_style, fmt.trim_trailing_whitespace — the named D7
exception). Both the style guide's multi_line_comment_layout form and the
documentation-header form with ` * ` prefixes. (Inside a procedure,
range-formatting a multi-line comment re-indents its interior lines, an
invariant failure reported separately.)
-- input.ssl --
/*
 * Procedure: Demo
 * Parameters:
 *   sInput   - the input string   
 *   nValue - a number
 * Returns: the processed result
;
/*
Recalculate the totals before the report runs.

    The report reads them without checking.
;
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:PARAMETERS sInput, nValue;
:RETURN sInput + LimsString(nValue);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/*
 * Procedure: Demo
 * Parameters:
 *   sInput   - the input string
 *   nValue - a number
 * Returns: the processed result
;
/*
Recalculate the totals before the report runs.

    The report reads them without checking.
;
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:PARAMETERS sInput, nValue;

	:RETURN sInput + LimsString(nValue);
:ENDPROC;
